Sorry - warning now - long post - but aren't most YAFAPs?? :)

I remember first playing rogue ... must have been 1985 or something
like that ... I could never get on the top 10 list (remember zippy the
zombie zapper?) although I had gotten "master rogue" a few times.
Usually I starved to death or found one of those phantom rooms and got
killed by one of those. At any rate, I started playing nethack around
last year.

I just played with nethack loaded into my hard drive, and I admit I
savescummed my way to a couple of ascensions. But I wanted to take the
challenge and do it without that crutch. As you can see from my
profile at alt.org/nethack I never really went very far. Mages find a
way to get hurt bigtime very early on in the game. The lack of food
doesn't help, either.

My last game I was on track for success. I had completed Sokoban and
the Mines and was on my way down, got SDSM through a wish by sitting
on a throne, and even negotiated my way through a Big Room. But I died
when I foolishly put away my lizard corpse and I encountered a
cockatrice on new moon (2 weeks ago, exactly) and it hissed. I was too
slow to get the lizard corpse out of my bag (and forgot praying was
probably faster) and died.

So it was with some trepidation that I started this new game. But you
know how it goes. You swear you won't play again because of the
frustration engendered, but it is all too tempting to go back and just
"play one more game and see how it goes."

This one was a doozy. I'm watching the ttyrecs because I didn't start
taking notes until it became clear that this character had a chance at
ascending, and those notes are on another computer (really!)

The beginning was not too special. It was nice that the scroll store
on level two, so I bought a bunch of ?oID so I didn't have to quaff /
read test most things early on. I encountered the early-game
starvation episode and had to go on a food dash, madly running down 3
levels in search of food, but survived that scare (by praying). What
was the real catalyst for success was the co-aligned altar on levels
2, I had acquired Magicbane at turn #2389 by offering a red mold
corpse (gee, if I can get Magicbane for mold, sure!). I tried altar
camping for a bit but gave up due to another hunger episode. I think
in retrospect Magicbane helped me kill a lot of monsters more powerful
than I during the early game, and that was the key to my survival.
Food was no longer an issue when the Oracle's floor was a bones level
with a bag containing a few rations.

I found and finished sokoban on DL7, got an "oR. Before I leave the
levels, I zap-test all the wands I had accumulated and one of them
turns out to be a /oWishing. So I wish for b?oC just in case. Good
wish - the wand happened to be 0:0 after that wish. After recharging
the wand, my next wish was for GDSM. Why GDSM? Noob mistake. My
rationale was that my [oMR might get burnt or rotted, but I did not
consider the MR conferred by Magicbane. Anyway, this would cost me
another wish later on. And given all the issues I had with starvation,
I wished for a =oSD. (1 wish I would have wanted back, because I found
one of those at a ring store in Minetown. Oh well.I had many more
things I wanted to wish for but decided to wait. It was about then
that I had a feeling this character would go far. Just needed to make
sure not to screw anything up.

The rest of the story ...

then went through the mines, found a BoH at the items store as well as
a B magic lamp. Got the luckstone.

found another co-aligned altar on level 11 and altar camped there for
a while, got a few spellbooks for the trouble.

My other wishes:
2 wishes for blessed scrolls of genocide (too many marker charges to
write) for h and L
1 wish for blessed rustproof helm of brilliance
2 wish for blessed magic markers

somewhere I had acquired an "oLS so I decided to swap out the
reflection for the life saving. To get the reflection back I exchanged
the GDSM for SDSM (from a silver dragon killed somewhere).

I had gotten to Medusa's level and scoured the levels for ='s. But no
=oLevit could be found, so that was my 10th wish.

Along the way, I had gotten stealth, which was great for the 3 throne
rooms and the (!) 3 leprechaun halls I had found. The loot from that,
as well as from Croesus, helped me get my AC down to -39 with the help
of the minetown priest. I also genocided c because they screwed up my
previous ascension attempt.

With the first two magic markers, I wrote the spellbooks that I needed
for my ascension. Charm monster, magic mapping, cure sickness (for
Juiblex), and extra healing, as well as ?oEA.

The castle was a cinch. I charmed a few dragons into being my pets,
which really took the heat off of me in the mazes. Minotaurs were not
difficult at all, either - they make great pets, too.

Somewhere along the line I found boots of speed (I need to look at my
notes to find out how), those were huge.

I expended quite a few turns with my pickaxe carving out straight
lines so my way up would be easier. The demon princes were easy, too,
I guess it was nice to have the straight lines carved out. With them
on the up stair, I waited 2 squares away and with my speed walked onto
the stair as soon as they teleported next to me to attack me. Really,
once you take away their ability to run upstairs and you have MR /
cold resistance (for Asmodeus), they are little kittens.

I went from exp level 15 up to exp 25 with the wraith corpses and ?
oGL's I had found. Even without wraith luring I got really lucky with
wraiths leaving corpses. My pets gobbled up a few of them, darn them.

Rodney is really easy when you give him the finger. I had a lot of
trouble with other roles without /oD when he started to summon storm,
steal my crap (once when a priest he stole my Mitre of Holiness, I
never went back to that game it was so frustrating).

On the way up I got too cute. I brought my pets (so many dragons,
jabberwocks, and minotaurs I called them my "cloud of electrons") up
with me and I figured I'd drop by the altars I had frequented in the
early game.

I lost some luck when Rodney came back, I thought it was safe to
finger him, but my pets were behind him. Darn pets getting in the
way.

I got REALLY too cute when I thought, "Hey, let's offer Rodney's
corpse to Thoth."

Oops. I had totally forgotten that nonchaotic gods get mad at you when
you offer your own race. I lost my 10 intrinsic protection points that
the leprechauns and Croesus had paid for and my AC was now a
"vulnerable" -29. I got SDSM to +4, but I noobishly forgot the "safe
zone" for item enchantment was +3, not +4. So I evaporated it when I
read a B?oEA.

Therefore, my next wish was for +2 SDSM to replace the one I had
stupidly destroyed.

1 more wish for a regular magic marker (so I could make U?oEA)

I used all my accumulated /o create monster, ?o CM, and my own CM
spell to make victims for sacrifice, but hurriedly abandoned that idea
when I created an Archon.

"Run away, run away" cried brave sir Robin!

I brought my pets (by then I had charmed a Ki-rin and an Angel from my
CM efforts above) with me to the planes. A crystal ball helped me find
the portals.

Earth was uneventful.

Air gave me a scare. At first glance, non of the E's were very close.
But I see this ...

"The umber hulk gazes. You get confused."

And then a whole lot of --More-- messages.

All the while the E's creep closer while I lose 10 (!!) turns ...

I get munched by an E and get to ~ 100 hp, which I know I can lose in
a hurry in the plane of air. So I used a ?oFH and kill the E. By then
my pets have stepped in to take care of the rest. Whew.

Fire and water were uneventful. The real heart attack special was the
astral plane.

Somehow during my sojourn through the dungeons I had only acquired 2
wands of teleportation. A TON of /oD, fire, lightning, etc. I used
telepathy to find the riders. Pestilence to the left, Death in center,
Famine to the right. I pick pestilence, teleporting the A's away and
fingering the @'s. I get to the left altar (blind) ... and do not see
the "sense of peace" message. (noobish retrospective: you don't see
that in the astral plane!!).

I head right, getting satiated to protect from famine, who I finger to
death. No "sense of peace" either.

Sigh, the altar must be in the center where Death is, but then I have
used up all of my teleport wand charges. My last wish, believe it or
not, was for a wand of teleportation (a kingdom for a horse! anyone?)
I skirt around Death, and get to the altar room. This must be it,
right? I get to the altar, and by this time I figure out not to "/"
the _, but to chat with the priest to figure out who it is.

With a sinking feeling, I discover the center altar is to Anhur. I
have to walk through the morass again?!?! 50/50 chance. At that time
my heart was pounding. I had worked on this character for 7 days, only
to lose it to a noobish mistake??

I guessed the altar to the right.

Well, thank goodness for my many wands of death and my two pet angels
and a pet djinni who sneaked in from the plane of water.

Getting past famine the second time wasn't so hard. And FINALLY I saw
"the priestess of Ptah turns to flee" I knew I was in the right room
(the 2nd time). When I chatted with the priestess on the right, she
gave me "2 bits for an ale" and I gave a massive sigh of relief.

Really, I was only close to dying 4 times this game - 2 near
drownings, the one I talked about above, and an incident with being
naked near a Titan (don't ask). In the astral plane, I used 3 of my 5
remaining blessed ?oFH, but mostly out of paranoia (150 hp or so) than
dire need. I also never used my 2 "oLS either.

So, without further ado ...

